<details><summary>Existing items (D1, D2, Q1)</summary>

- Q1 ([comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13268#issuecomment-6913988968), [JinDX](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13268#issuecomment-6919288876)): Decided on Option b (not applied on the PR branch yet).
- D1 ([comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13268#issuecomment-6913988968)): Yes, D1 is separate from Option b — `b2` is still `new focus target`, so if a `blur` listener adopts `b2` into a navigating same-origin `<iframe>`, step 4.1 resolves `document` to the `<iframe>`'s `Document`, designates `b2` as its focused area, and sets its `focus changed during ongoing navigation` to true. Not applied: proposed fix ([spec](https://github.com/noamr/html/tree/spec-review/html-13268/d1), [tests](https://github.com/noamr/wpt/tree/spec-review/html-13268/d1)). Minimal repro:

  ```js
  // Inside a document with focus, with a same-origin `iframe` containing `<button autofocus>`:
  b1.focus();
  childWin.navigation.addEventListener("navigate", e => {
    e.intercept({ handler: () => promise, focusReset: "after-transition" });
  }, { once: true });
  const finished = childWin.navigation.navigate("#1").finished;

  b1.addEventListener("blur", () => childDoc.body.appendChild(b2), { once: true });
  b2.focus();
  // Spec (even with Option b): childDoc's focused area becomes b2 and its focus-changed flag becomes true.
  // Chromium & Gecko: childDoc is not focused, and resolving `promise` still resets focus to childAutofocus.
  ```

- D2 ([comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13268#issuecomment-6913988968)): Cross-frame WPT coverage. Not applied: proposed fix ([tests](https://github.com/noamr/wpt/tree/spec-review/html-13268/d2)).
</details>

